#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""pc-bot: your PC reports to you on Telegram.

  pc-bot setup                  connect a Telegram bot (asks for the token)
  pc-bot run                    the background service (systemd starts it)
  pc-bot send [--important] TEXT   send an event from a script or hook
  pc-bot claude                 Claude Code hook: reads the hook's JSON on stdin
  pc-bot test                   send a test message
  pc-bot mode [all|away|quiet]  show or change what gets sent
  pc-bot lockdown               turn off all remote control now
  pc-bot unlock                 lift a lockdown (asks your sudo password for root)
  pc-bot session [MINUTES]      how long one code keeps the bot unlocked (default 60)
  pc-bot claude-dir [PATH]      the folder Claude works in (default: your home)
  pc-bot update                 pull the latest version and restart

Security (after `sudo root/setup.sh` from this folder): Claude, screenshots,
windows and /say need the bot unlocked with a code from your authenticator app
(an hour by default, `pc-bot session` changes it); /sudo needs a fresh code per command, checked by a root-owned
helper that holds the secret. Five wrong codes lock everything down.

Your own chats (Telegram Business): connect the bot in Settings, Telegram
Business, Chatbots. New messages in the chats you pick arrive as cards with a
reply Claude wrote in your voice (Send, Another, Skip; reply to the card to say
what to answer); auto-reply per person. That Claude has no tools. /inbox.

Talk to Claude from the bot's chat: type, send a voice note (transcribed with
Superwhisper) or a photo. Replies stream live as Telegram rich messages, with a
stop button, and can carry a visual card (a Telegram widget). /look (default)
lets Claude read and search only; /work runs Claude Code in auto mode.

Modes:
  away   (default) everyday events only while you're away: screen locked or
         the screensaver on. Important ones (wrong passwords, low battery,
         the PC turning on, strangers messaging the bot) always come.
  all    everything, always.
  quiet  important events only.

Only the chat that ran setup can talk to the bot. Messages use Telegram rich
formatting (Bot API 10.1+) and fall back to plain text if that ever fails.
"""

